  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a large +10.6 pt gain over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, 0.485 acc), confirming that multiprofile structure carries substantial signal. However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool). Uncertainty: it is unknown whether a transformer-based aggregation, which can model cell-to-cell relationships within a profile, can further exploit the multiprofile structure beyond simple averaging. This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly one variable—aggregation (transformer vs avgpool)—while holding model setting, profile setting, and RNA encoder (pca_n2000) constant, making it a clean comparison. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly extends our strongest result with a single, well-motivated change; if transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool, it identifies a high-value design axis to build on, and if it does not, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can redirect effort toward encoder choice or multimodal fusion without having wasted an experiment on a confounded comparison."
}

